  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;The principle of development it would fail to achieve a\r\nsustainable form of development in that it is insufficient in original size to\r\nbe converted and would result in the loss of a family-sized unit (Class C3) to\r\nwhich there is a shortfall of this mix of housing within the Borough therefore\r\nundermining the ability to meet the Borough&#x27;s housing need and demand both\r\ncurrently and in the future contrary to the NPPF (2024) and Policies 1, 15 and\r\n20 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;\r\n\r\n&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;The application compromises insufficient information with\r\nregard to refuse and recycling, as without further information, if the bins are\r\nto be kept as existing, the bins being un-enclosed within a bin store and their\r\nlocation immediately outside the window of Bedroom 1, officers consider that\r\nthe proposed waste arrangements would result in an unacceptable living\r\nenvironment to the occupiers of bedroom 1 contrary to Policies 57 and 93 of the\r\nadopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024) and the Council’s Waste &amp;amp;\r\nRecycling Policy for Developers (September 2022).&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
